4, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01U9FgSfXfwCJSxTbFrAaycB", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 373240, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The nightly failure is fixed and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Fix:** I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, commit 08d3cd5986. I checked both test values by hand: 2.675 gives 2.68 and 2.665 gives 2.66.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge it. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test file to see what the test expects.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CYXE9ax8G8odWRdb2FK4ib", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017FdsJ489d3vLtAD3hQgRDW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked the test values against half-even: 2.675 rounds to 2.68 (7 is odd, so it goes up to the even digit) and 2.665 rounds to 2.66 (6 is even, so it stays). The test is correct, so only the source needs to change. I'll create the branch and commit the fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "to