": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01U9FgSfXfwCJSxTbFrAaycB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "Fixes the nightly build failure in tests/test_money.py.\n\n`round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). This switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nVerified against the test expectations:\n- 2.675 -> 2.68 (half-even rounds to the even digit 8)\n- 2.665 -> 2.66 (half-even rounds to the even digit 6)\n\nCI run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-banker-rounding-fin-212", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Fix:** I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, commit 08d3cd5986. I checked both test values by hand: 2.675 gives 2.68 and 2.665 gives 2.66.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI did not merge it. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}